  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Louisiana received $92M in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. Obligations are down 98.5% year over year. The state has 917 awards so far with an average award size of $100K. These totals are partial because current-year totals are fiscal year to date. Recent fiscal-year history shows much larger annual obligations: FY22 was $3.7B, FY23 was $4.5B, FY24 was $3.9B, FY25 was $5B, and FY26 was $5.9B. Facilities Support Services is the largest industry in FY2027 to date with $41.4M in obligations. The Department of Energy is the top buying agency in FY2027 to date with $31.9M in obligations. STRATEGIC STORAGE PARTNERS, LLC. is the top vendor in FY2027 to date with $31M in obligations.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How does FY2027 to date compare with prior fiscal years?",
        "body": "FY2027 to date obligations are $92M, a sharp decline from prior full-year totals. FY22 obligations were $3.7B, FY23 obligations were $4.5B, FY24 obligations were $3.9B, FY25 obligations were $5B, and FY26 obligations were $5.9B. Obligations are down 98.5% year over year, and current-year totals are partial because they are fiscal year to date."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies, vendors, and industries drive FY2027 to date spending?",
        "body": "The Department of Energy leads buying agencies with $31.9M in obligations, followed by the Department of Veterans Affairs with $25M and NASA with $10.5M. STRATEGIC STORAGE PARTNERS, LLC. is the top vendor with $31M, followed by NOVA SPACE SOLUTIONS, LLC with $8.7M and ALPHA MARINE SERVICES LLC with $5.4M. Facilities Support Services is the largest industry by obligations with $41.4M, followed by Navigational Services to Shipping with $5.4M and Temporary Help Services with $4.2M."
      }
    ]
  },
